  1. Create a user

  curl -X POST http://localhost:8888/api/users \
    -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
    -d '{"name": "Alice"}'

  ---
  2. Add product to cart

  curl -X POST http://localhost:8888/api/users/1/cart \
    -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
    -d '{"productId": 1, "quantity": 2}'
  ▎ Replace 1 in the path with the id returned from step 1, and productId with an existing product ID from your inventory.

  ---
  3. Place order

  curl -X POST http://localhost:8888/api/users/1/orders \
    -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
    -d '{
      "warehouseId": 1,
      "deliveryAddress": {
        "street": "123 Main St",
        "city": "New York",
        "state": "NY",
        "zipCode": "10001",
        "country": "US"
      },
      "paymentType": "CASH"
    }'
  ▎ paymentType accepts "CASH" or "CREDIT_CARD". warehouseId must match an existing warehouse.

  ---
  4. View orders

  All orders for a user:
  curl http://localhost:8888/api/users/1/orders

  Single order by ID:
  curl http://localhost:8888/api/orders/1

  ---
  Bonus — other useful curls

  Remove a product from cart:
  curl -X DELETE http://localhost:8888/api/users/1/cart/1

  Empty the cart:
  curl -X DELETE http://localhost:8888/api/users/1/cart

  All orders (admin view):
  curl http://localhost:8888/api/orders

  Check user profile:
  curl http://localhost:8888/api/users/1/profile
